{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most expensive tax you will ever \npay is not collected by the IRS.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6800,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It does not show up on your payub and your \naccountant probably has no idea it even exists.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14080,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I call it the I deserve it tax. It is a massive \nfinancial penalty levied against your net worth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22760,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here is the catch. You \nare the one signing the check.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We usually think of financial failure as a \nlack of knowledge or a lack of discipline.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34520,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We assume that if we just read one more \nbook on index funds, everything will click.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40680,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have realized that most of our worst \nfinancial decisions do not happen in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45280,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prefrontal cortex where logic lives. They \nhappen in the survival centers of the brain.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52800,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you are burnt out, exhausted, \nand feeling like a cog in a machine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57840,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your biology actually tricks you into sabotaging \nyour future. Today, we are going to look at the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65240,
    "dDurationMs": 8920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "neuroscience of why a bad week at work can cost \nyou $300,000 in 30 years. Before we dive into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74160,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the gray matter, let's set the stage. Think about \nthe last time you had a truly soul crushing week.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82520,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe your boss is a nightmare, or you have \nbeen staring at spreadsheets for 10 hours a day.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88920,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On Friday night, you find yourself browsing for \na luxury watch or a new car you do not need,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94840,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinking the phrase, \"I deserve this.\" \nThat is the I deserve it tax in action.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102640,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a biological demand for relief that \nmanifests as an irrational financial choice.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109520,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to stop paying this tax and \nactually keep the money you suffer for,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hit that subscribe button. Consider it a high \nyield investment in your own financial psychology.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121320,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I try to make sure every minute you spend here \npays dividends in your bank account later. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127880,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's look at why your brain starts acting like \nyour own worst enemy the moment you get stressed.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134040,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand the I deserve attacks, we \nhave to look at the biology of burnout.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2019, the World Health Organization officially \nlabeled burnout as an occupational phenomenon.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146400,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what is actually happening under the hood? \nWhen you deal with chronic workplace stress,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152040,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your brain's amygdala, which is basically your \ninternal fire alarm, is constantly ringing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158800,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This triggers the HPA axis, which stands for the \nhypothalamic pituitary adrenal axis. This system  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166480,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "floods your body with cortisol and adrenaline. \nIn short bursts, this is great for finishing a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171880,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "report by midnight. But when it becomes chronic, \ncortisol becomes neurotoxic. It is like leaving  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179120,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your car's engine redlinining for 3 weeks \nstraight. Eventually, things start to break.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the first thing that breaks in a stressed out \nprofessional is the ability to think long term.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your brain stops being a wealth-b buildinging \nmachine and starts being a survival machine. It  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197160,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is not interested in your retirement account. It \nis interested in making the pain stop right now.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203880,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The physical reality of this is actually \nterrifying. Research from organizations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the APA shows that chronic stress literally \nshrinks the connections in your prefrontal cortex.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215000,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I like to call the prefrontal cortex \nyour wealthb buildinging center.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219400,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the part of your brain responsible \nfor executive function, impulse control,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224000,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and understanding compound interest. It is the \nlogical adult in the room. When you are burnt out,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230920,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that adult is basically tied up in the basement. \nMeanwhile, the more primitive parts of your brain,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the strriatam and the amydala, take the \nsteering wheel. These parts of the brain do not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242480,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understand that a $60,000 car loan will take six \nyears to pay off. They only understand that the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249160,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leather seats feel soft and the new car smell \nmakes the bad feelings go away for 15 minutes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are literally making financial \ndecisions with a damaged brain architecture.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260560,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why even smart high earning professionals \ncan end up broke. Their biology has hijacked their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267160,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "balance sheet and they are essentially \nshopping under the influence of cortisol.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the key markers of burnout is cynicism. \nYou start to feel a mental distance from your job.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278640,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You feel like your work doesn't matter \nand your time is being stolen from you.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This creates a psychological vacuum \nthat we try to fill with stuff.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289040,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you feel like you have no agency at \nwork, you try to reclaim it through spending.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where the term revenge spending comes \nfrom. It is a retaliation against a system  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300120,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that makes you feel small. You think \nif I have to endure this terrible job,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305960,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am at least going to have the best \nkitchen appliances or a designer wardrobe.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311320,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a way of proving to yourself that you are \nstill in control. But it is an expensive illusion.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318480,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every time you spend money to spite your job, you \nare actually giving that job more power over you.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325240,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are trading your future freedom \nfor a temporary feeling of defiance.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330440,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most dangerous part of this biological shift \nis how it messes with your perception of time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337080,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A healthy brain can look 20 years into the future \nand see the benefit of a diversified portfolio.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343720,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A burntout brain has a time horizon of about \n48 hours. This is called time discounting.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When your survival brain is in charge, the future \nfeels like a fantasy that might never happen.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358240,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All that matters is the acute stress of today. \nThis is why people who are otherwise brilliant  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364080,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with numbers will suddenly make an impulsive \n$5,000 purchase on a Tuesday night. They aren't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370800,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being stupid. They are being biological. \nTheir brain has decided that the long-term  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "benefit of that money is less valuable than the \nimmediate neurochemical relief of a purchase.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383120,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To fix your finances, you have to first recognize \nthat your brain is lying to you about what you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388440,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually need. You don't need a new gadget. \nYou need a nervous system that isn't on fire.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you think the physical shrinking \nof your executive brain is bad,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400320,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wait until you see what burnout \ndoes to your dopamine levels.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405120,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most people think dopamine is about pleasure, \nbut that is a myth that is costing you a fortune  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410600,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every single year. In a moment, I'm going \nto explain why the buy now button on Amazon  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually acting like a syringe for your \nbrain and how that one chemical keeps you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423240,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coming back for depreciating liabilities even \nwhen you know better. We have to look at the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429680,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dopamine deficit hypothesis to understand why \nwe seek rewards that actually make us poorer.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437000,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have ever wondered why the thrill of a new \npurchase disappears the moment you open the box,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442800,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the answer is hidden in the way \nyour brain anticipates a reward.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447480,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's get into the neuroscience \nof the dopamine trap.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451320,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to clear something up about dopamine. Most \npeople think it is the chemical of reward or joy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458880,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It isn't. Dopamine is the chemical \nof motivation and anticipation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464880,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the brain's way of saying, \"Hey, pay \nattention. Something potentially good is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469480,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about to happen.\" When you are burnt out, your \nbaseline dopamine levels are in the basement.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475960,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The things that usually bring you joy, like a \nhobby or spending time with friends, require  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481040,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too much energy. Your brain is starving for a \nwin, and it wants the path of least resistance.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488520,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the modern world, the easiest way to get \na dopamine spike is frictionless consumerism.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don't have to train for a marathon or learn \na new skill. You just have to tap a screen.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500680,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The act of browsing and the act of clicking \npurchase releases a surge of dopamine  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that makes you feel alive again for a fleeting \nsecond. But notice I said the act of buying,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511760,
    "dDurationMs": 8040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the act of owning. This is the cruel irony of \nthe I deserve it tax. The neurochemical high peaks  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519800,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you are waiting for the package to arrive. \nIt is the anticipation that provides the relief.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526440,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once the item is actually in your hands, the \ndopamine levels crash back down to baseline or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531920,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "often even lower. This is why you have boxes from \nonline retailers sitting unopened in your hallway  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538920,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or why that new tech gadget is \ngathering dust after 3 days.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You didn't actually want the item. You wanted \nthe dopamine hit that came with the transaction.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549000,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This creates a psychological dependency because \nthe underlying problem, your job burnout,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554640,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hasn't been solved. Your brain demands another \nfix. You are essentially self-medicating with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560920,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retail therapy. Every time you pay the I deserve \nit tax, you are just buying another temporary  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566680,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dose of neurochemical normaly. It is a cycle that \nkeeps you broke and keeps the corporations rich.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All because your brain is looking \nfor a shortcut to feeling okay.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578320,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is also a social component to \nthis revenge spending. As humans,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are social primates and we are hardwired \nto care about our status within the tribe.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chronic stress at work often makes us \nfeel undervalued and unappreciated.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594160,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When your boss treats you like a line item, your \nserotonin levels drop. To compensate, you look for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600080,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ways to signal status to the world. This is why \nwe are drawn to visible depreciating liabilities.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606920,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An index fund is a fantastic asset, but you \ncannot wear it to a party and you cannot park  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612160,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it in your driveway. You can't show it to the \npeople who make you feel small. So, you buy the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618120,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "luxury car or the designer bag. It is a biological \nattempt to purchase respect and social standing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625600,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are trying to use money to solve a feeling of \ninadequacy. The problem is that the people you are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to impress are usually too busy worrying \nabout their own status to even notice yours. You  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are sacrificing your financial freedom to buy a \nstatus signal that nobody is actually looking at.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644120,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The marketing industry has become incredibly good \nat weaponizing the language of mental health.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650240,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have taken the concept of self-care and \nturned it into a reason to buy things. We are told  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656600,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that an expensive vacation, a luxury candle, or a \nhigh-end skin care routine is an act of self-love.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664680,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have a different perspective. True \nself-care isn't a depreciating liability.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670960,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "True self-care is having an emergency fund \nso you don't have to stay at a toxic job.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677120,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "True self-care is having assets that \ngenerate income so you can reclaim your time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683800,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we conflate consumerism with mental \nhealth, we are falling for a lie that keeps  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688560,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us on the treadmill. Every time you buy into the \ntreat yourself narrative to cope with burnout,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are actually making it harder to escape \nthe situation that is burning you out.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700720,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have to learn to distinguish between genuine \nrelief and a marketing tactic designed to exploit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706520,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our exhaustion. Now, we are getting to the really \ndangerous part. If you don't break this cycle,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713440,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you end up in a situation that finance people call \nthe golden handcuffs. Most people think they will  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719800,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just earn their way out of stress. They think if I \nget that next promotion, I will finally be happy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what actually happens is that as your \nincome rises, your stress rises and your I  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deserve it tax increases right along with it. \nIn a moment, I am going to show you the math  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how a single luxury car payment can literally \ntrap you in a job you hate for an extra decade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the mechanism that turns successful \nprofessionals into highincome prisoners.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to know how to spot \nthe trap before it snaps shut,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to talk about the math of depreciating \nliabilities and the prison of lifestyle creep.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759240,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Behavioral economists have a term \nfor this, the hedonic treadmill.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It describes our tendency to return to a stable \nlevel of happiness regardless of what we buy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769240,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or achieve. When you get that $60,000 BMW, \nit feels like a dream for the first month.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the third month, it is just your \ncar. You have habituated to the luxury.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is that while your happiness \nhas returned to its baseline, your financial  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786560,
    "dDurationMs": 7880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obligation has stayed at $900 a month. This is \nthe foundation of the I deserve it tax trap. You  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increase your cost of living to cope with stress, \nbut the new stuff quickly stops providing relief.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800200,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To get the same high, you have to buy something \neven bigger and even more expensive. Meanwhile,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806120,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have to keep working that high stress job just \nto maintain the baseline you have already built.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811720,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have essentially outsourced \nyour happiness to your creditors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814960,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they are charging a very high interest rate. \nLet me tell you about a guy I knew named David.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822200,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David was a high-erforming attorney making \n300,000 a year, but he was absolutely miserable.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828840,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To cope with the 80hour weeks, \nhe justified a massive lifestyle.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had the $5,000 a month penthouse \nand the high-end watch collection.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He told himself he deserved these \nthings because of how hard he worked.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842960,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here is what happened when he finally hit a \nwall and wanted to quit. He looked at his bills  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and realized he couldn't leave. His depreciating \nliabilities had formed a set of golden handcuffs.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856360,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was legally and financially bound to the very \njob that was destroying his health because he had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862000,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spent all his ammunition on things that were \nlosing value. He was a wealthy man on paper,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867960,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he had zero freedom. This is the ultimate \ngoal of the I deserve it tax. It doesn't just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874960,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take your money. It takes your options. It ensures \nthat you are too broke to ever tell your boss no.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882480,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David's story is a warning that a high \nincome is not the same thing as wealth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888280,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another reason we fall into this trap is ego \ndepletion. Research suggests that willpower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895240,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a finite resource. Every decision you \nmake at work, from what to say in a meeting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901560,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to how to phrase an email, drains your mental \nbattery. By the time you get home at 7:00 p.m.,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908960,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your prefrontal cortex is completely exhausted. \nThis is when you are most vulnerable.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916040,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a targeted ad for a new pair of shoes or \na piece of tech pops up on your feed, you don't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922200,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the energy to mount a logical defense. \nThe friction required to say no is too high.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930200,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why financial success is rarely about \nwillpower. It is about systems. If you rely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937360,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on your brain to make good choices when you are \ntired, you are going to lose every single time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944520,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The modern economy is specifically designed to \ncatch you when you are depleted. It waits for that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950960,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moment of weakness to sell you a depreciating \nliability under the guise of a reward.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957880,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We also suffer from something called mental \naccounting. This is a concept developed by Richard  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963440,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thaylor. We treat money differently depending \non where it came from or how we feel about it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you feel like you have suffered for your \npaycheck, you unconsciously put that money into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975280,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a survival or entertainment bucket. You don't \nsee it as a neutral tool for building wealth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981960,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see it as a trophy that must be redeemed for \na prize. This emotional attachment to the money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "makes you more likely to spend it irrationally. \nYou feel that because you earned it through pain,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994840,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should spend it on pleasure. But the \nmath doesn't care about your feelings.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000760,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A dollar invested while you are happy grows at \nthe same rate as a dollar invested while you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005760,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are miserable. The trick is learning to see \nyour income as a tool for your future self,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011920,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not just a bandage for your current \nself. So, how do we fix this?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You cannot willpower your way out of biological \nexhaustion. So, you have to build guard rails.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024160,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first and most effective strategy is the 48 \nhour dopamine delay rule. Here is how it works.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031320,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For any non-essential purchase over $100, you \nmust wait two full days before hitting buy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037840,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a neuroscientific hack. You still get \nthe dopamine spike of browsing and adding the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "item to your cart. You have satisfied \nthe immediate craving for the hit,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047000,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but by closing the browser and walking away, \nyou allow the acute emotional surge to subside.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You give your prefrontal cortex time to come \nback online and evaluate the purchase logically.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058320,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have found that about 80% of the things \nI think I need on a stressful Tuesday night  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062840,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look completely ridiculous by Thursday \nmorning. This rule alone can save you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067440,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of dollars a year. It isn't about \nsaying no. It is about saying not right now.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073880,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a way of letting the biological storm pass \nbefore you make a permanent financial decision.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079600,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next step is to reframe \nwhat a reward actually is.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084120,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The I deserve it narrative is very strong and you \nshouldn't try to silence it. Instead, redirect it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092320,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You do deserve to be rewarded for your hard \nwork, but you need to redefine the prize.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098440,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of rewarding yourself with a \ndepreciating liability that keeps you trapped,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102960,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reward yourself with freedom. When you feel the \nurge to spend $300 on something you don't need,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110120,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "log into your brokerage account and buy $300 \nof an index fund instead. Look at the share  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116720,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "count and say to yourself, I am buying my future \ntime. I am buying my escape route from this job.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124760,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am buying my autonomy. You have to train your \nbrain to get a dopamine hit from accumulating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131320,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assets rather than acquiring liabilities. It takes \ntime, but eventually watching your net worth grow  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138920,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "becomes more satisfying than any luxury purchase \ncould ever be. You are still treating yourself.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146080,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are just treating your future self \ninstead of a corporate shareholder.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150760,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If decision fatigue is the enemy, then automation \nis your greatest ally. You need to make your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156600,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wealth-b buildinging decisions at a time when you \nare rested and clearheaded. Set up your 401k, your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163200,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Roth IRA, and your brokerage transfers to happen \nautomatically the moment your paycheck hits.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169280,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The goal is to make sure the money for your future \nnever even touches your checking account. By the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1174680,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time you are sitting on the couch on a Friday \nnight, exhausted and looking for something to buy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179480,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the money for your freedom is already gone. It is \nsafely tucked away in your investment accounts.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186240,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This artificially restricts the amount of capital \navailable for the I deserve it tax. It is much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192200,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "harder to overspend when the money isn't there to \nbegin with. You are essentially bypassing your own  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197880,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depleted brain and letting a system handle \nthe heavy lifting of building your wealth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's run the hard numbers on the \nopportunity cost of revenge spending.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208800,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine burnout convinces you that you deserve \na new luxury car with a $900 monthly payment.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over 5 years, that car will cost \nyou $54,000 in payments alone.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221280,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at the end, it will be \nworth a fraction of that.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what happens if you invest that $900 a \nmonth into a diversified index fund instead  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232160,
    "dDurationMs": 8280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at an 8% return? After 5 years, you would have \nroughly $66,000. If you then just left that money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240440,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alone to grow for another 20 years, it would \nballoon to over $300,000. When you look at that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248120,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "car, you shouldn't see leather seats and a logo. \nYou should see a $300,000 hole in your retirement.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you realize that your treat is \nactually an act of financial self-sabotage,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261760,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it loses its appeal very quickly. The I \ndeserve it tax is literally the difference  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268600,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between retiring in your 50s or working \nuntil you are 70. Once you see the math,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the luxury item doesn't look like a reward \nanymore. It looks like a prison sentence.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281920,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your logical brain is finally back in charge. At \nthe end of the day, financial independence is not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1288280,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just about having a high net worth. It is about \nhaving agency over your time and your biology.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The I deserve it tax is a symptom \nof a life that is out of balance.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to dive deeper into these strategies \nand join a community of people who are hacking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their way to freedom, consider clicking the join \nbutton below to become one of the optimizers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our members get custom sketch badges and priority \nreplies on comments, but more importantly, they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314880,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are committed to peerreviewing their financial \nhabits and sharing data. We are building a culture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320760,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where we value assets over status. The road to \nwealth is paved with the things you did not buy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1327920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stop paying the I deserve it tax to \ncorporations and start paying it to yourself.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332920,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
